  "summary": "# Health-Tech Daily Digest — November 18, 2026\n\nThe White House withdrew its nomination of Heidi Overton for FDA commissioner following criticism from both GOP and MAHA leaders over her record on vaping regulation, leaving the agency's leadership in continued flux. Meanwhile, federal regulators moved to strengthen patient data privacy and control, with HHS updating HIPAA rules to support patient access to medical records through health apps, and the FDA releasing a new AI roadmap through CMS to guide responsible deployment of artificial intelligence in healthcare. On the clinical innovation front, startups are advancing next-generation treatments across multiple domains: Marrow Therapeutics secured $173 million for a novel delivery approach to blood disorder drugs, Sellas reported positive phase-trial results for blood cancer immunotherapy, and researchers made progress on safer gene therapy methods following a prior patient death. The U.S. lost its measles elimination status—a notable public health setback—while China Medical University Hospital demonstrated AI's immediate clinical value by reducing cardiac ischemia detection time, and domestic health systems reported operational gains from virtual nursing and AI-assisted prior authorization tools.",
